{
  "_meta": {
    "purpose": "Canonical PT/EN base-name per cycle theme token. Used by the naming pipeline to keep names consistent across sets.",
    "schema": "themeToken -> { en, pt, g?, review? }. en/pt are the canonical PLURAL cycle name. g is the PT grammatical gender of the head noun ('m' default, 'f' explicit) and drives adjective agreement. review:true = PT is a guess; every cycle using this base is flagged ptReview:true.",
    "policy": "EN uses the community cycle name. PT uses the OFFICIAL printed Portuguese term when one exists (spell=mágica, sorcery=feitiço, instant=mágica instantânea, enchantment=encantamento, land=terreno, creature=criatura, artifact=artefato, flash=Lampejo, flashback=Flashback, mutate=Mutar, storm=Tempestade); otherwise keeps the English term (Leylines, Gearhulks, Myojin, Zubera, Baku, Genju, Charms, Slivers). Set suffix is applied by the pipeline, not stored here.",
    "qualifierSchema": "_qualifiers[k] -> { en, pt, kind?, review? }. pt as a string is invariable ('de duas cores'); pt as an object is { ms, fs, mp, fp } and agrees with the head noun. kind:'rarity' moves the adjective to the end in PT and joins multiple rarities with ' e '."
  },

